<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
<title>Facility Build Costs — Spacemolt KB</title>
<script>(function(){try{var t=localStorage.getItem('smkb-theme');if(!t){t=window.matchMedia&&window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: light)').matches?'light':'dark';}document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme',t);}catch(e){}})();</script>
<style>
:root{--bg:#0d1117;--panel:#161b22;--panel2:#1c2128;--border:#30363d;--border2:#21262d;--text:#c9d1d9;--muted:#8b949e;--muted2:#6e7681;--dim:#adbac7;--link:#58a6ff;--link2:#1f6feb;--accent:#e3b341;--accent2:#d29922;--accent3:#9a6700;--up:#3fb950;--up2:#2ea043;--down:#f85149;--purple:#6c5ce7;--grid:#6e7681}
:root[data-theme="light"]{--bg:#ffffff;--panel:#f6f8fa;--panel2:#eaeef2;--border:#d0d7de;--border2:#d8dee4;--text:#1f2328;--muted:#656d76;--muted2:#8c959f;--dim:#57606a;--link:#0969da;--link2:#0969da;--accent:#9a6700;--accent2:#9a6700;--accent3:#7d4e00;--up:#1a7f37;--up2:#1a7f37;--down:#cf222e;--purple:#6639ba;--grid:#afb8c1}
.theme-toggle{position:fixed;top:.5rem;right:.5rem;z-index:10;background:var(--panel);color:var(--text);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:6px;padding:.3rem .55rem;font-size:1rem;cursor:pointer;line-height:1}
.theme-toggle:hover{border-color:var(--link)}

 body{font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;margin:0;padding:1rem;background:var(--bg);color:var(--text)}
 a{color:var(--link)} h1{margin:.3rem 0} h2{margin:1.6rem 0 .3rem;font-size:1.15rem} h3{margin:0 0 .2rem;font-size:.95rem}
 .legend{font-size:.85rem;color:var(--muted);max-width:80ch}
 .cards{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.6rem;margin-top:1rem}
 .card{display:block;min-width:8rem;background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:6px;padding:.7rem .9rem;color:var(--text);text-decoration:none}
 .card:hover{border-color:var(--link)}
 .card .n{font-size:1.5rem;color:var(--accent);line-height:1}
 .card .g{text-transform:capitalize;margin-top:.2rem}
 .explainer p{max-width:80ch;font-size:.9rem;color:var(--text);margin:.4rem 0}
 code{background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:3px;padding:0 .25rem;font-size:.85em}
 .statblocks{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:1rem 1.6rem;margin-top:.6rem}
 .statblock{min-width:22rem}
 .statblock h3 .g{text-transform:capitalize;color:var(--accent)} .statblock h3 small{color:var(--muted);font-weight:400}
 table{border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.8rem;margin:.2rem 0 .4rem}
 th,td{border:1px solid var(--border2);padding:.25rem .5rem;text-align:right} th:first-child,td:first-child{text-align:left}
 td.dash{color:var(--muted2)}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<button type="button" class="theme-toggle" title="Toggle light/dark theme" aria-label="Toggle light/dark theme" onclick="(function(){var r=document.documentElement,t=r.getAttribute('data-theme')==='light'?'dark':'light';r.setAttribute('data-theme',t);try{localStorage.setItem('smkb-theme',t);}catch(e){}})()">◐</button>
<p><a href="../">← Build Costs</a></p>
<h1>Facility Build Costs</h1>
<p class="legend">Cost to <strong>construct</strong> each facility, two ways: <strong>BoM (ore)</strong> flattens the build to raw materials; <strong>Recipe (components)</strong> uses the direct build components. Each is priced by <strong>MKT-AVG</strong> (sell-side volume-weighted average) and <strong>Galaxy</strong> (cheapest sourcing, walking pooled sell-order depth across every station). Production facilities are grouped by what they produce; others by facility type.</p>
<div class="cards">
{{range .Summaries}}<a class="card" href="{{.Href}}"><div class="n">{{.Count}}</div><div class="g">{{.Group}}</div></a>
{{end}}</div>

<section class="explainer">
<h2>How to read the two prices</h2>
<p><strong>MKT-AVG</strong> is the sell-side volume-weighted average of <em>past trades</em> (price × quantity). It shows a value for any component that has <em>ever</em> traded, whether or not it is for sale right now, and does <em>not</em> check current supply — a "typical cost" estimate.</p>
<p><strong>Galaxy</strong> walks the <em>current</em> resting sell orders pooled across every station, filling cheapest-first until the required quantity is met. It is all-or-nothing per component: when a component cannot be fully sourced from live depth it shows <code>—</code>, and the build-cost line shows <code>N/M covered</code>. A large gap between the two columns means a facility is priceable in theory but not actually sourceable from the market right now.</p>
</section>

<section class="stats">
<h2>Category stats</h2>
<p class="legend"><strong>Median</strong> MKT-AVG build cost by facility level, with the full <strong>(min–max)</strong> range in parentheses, and how many facilities are <strong>currently buildable</strong> (inputs fully sourceable from live galaxy depth via BoM or Recipe). The median with a min–max range is shown rather than mean ± sd because costs within a level are strongly right-skewed — most facilities cluster low, with a thin tail of far pricier end-game variants — so a mean would sit well above the typical facility. Cost stats cover facilities with a fully-priced bill, so a level's count may exceed the number priced; <code>—</code> means none at that level are fully priced.</p>
<div class="statblocks">
{{range .Stats}}<div class="statblock">
<h3><span class="g">{{.Group}}</span> <small>{{.Count}}</small></h3>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Lvl</th><th>#</th><th>BoM MKT median (min–max)</th><th>Recipe MKT median (min–max)</th><th>Buildable now</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{{range .Levels}}<tr><td>L{{.Level}}</td><td>{{.Count}}</td><td{{if eq .BoM "—"}} class="dash"{{end}}>{{.BoM}}</td><td{{if eq .Recipe "—"}} class="dash"{{end}}>{{.Recipe}}</td><td>{{.Buildable}}</td></tr>
{{end}}</tbody>
</table>
</div>
{{end}}</div>
</section>
</body>
</html>
